.venv314/

# Personal Claude Code permissions, never shared
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local-only captured RF codes (device-specific, not for publication)
docs/*-codes-manual.md

# Outbound reply drafts. A reply already posted lives in its thread, along with
# what it was answering — a copy here is a fork that drifts in silence. Worse,
# .claude/commands/support-issue.md reads docs/ as reference material, so a stale
# draft becomes input to a future triage. Draft in a scratch directory instead;
# `gh issue comment --body-file -` takes the text on stdin and needs no file.
docs/reply-*.md
docs/post-*.md
